  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Many users use tools like OVR or GoLoco to move their character around to accomodate certain social situations. Historically, this does *not* move the actual pill bounding box that the user is based around, but it does move things like the nameplate.\n\nHowever, the chatbox seems to be bound to a layer between the avatar model and the bounding pill. The result is that if the user has \"top\" instead of \"middle\" chatboxes selected, the chatbox can be occluded by the user's avatar if they are using GoLoco. This is not an issue for OVR however. \n\nAttached is a visual example of me using GoLoco on desktop. I am not expecting this to be necessarily fixed since it seems to be a less common issue and it only would affect users using GoLoco with the height adjusted.",
